Update the API Catalog page filtering mechanism to replace the existing category-based filters (Payments, Mobile, Accounts & Orders) with a new domain-based multi-select filter. The new filter should allow users to filter APIs by multiple domain categories while maintaining the existing View All and Favorites functionality.
h2. Current State
h3. Existing Filter Options
 * *View All* - Shows all APIs (default selected, black chip)
 * *Favorites* - Shows favorited APIs (gray chip)
 * *Payments* - Category filter (gray chip)
 * *Mobile* - Category filter (gray chip)
 * *Accounts & Orders* - Category filter (gray chip)

h3. Current Behavior
 * Single-select filter chips (only one can be active at a time)
 * Active filter displays as black chip, inactive as gray
 * No multi-select capability
 * No domain-based filtering

h2. New Requirements
h3. New Filter Structure

Replace category filters with a domain-based multi-select dropdown:

*Filter Options:*
 # *View All* (existing, keep as-is)
 # *Favorites* (existing, keep as-is)
 # *Domain* (NEW - multi-select dropdown)

h3. Domain Options (Dynamic)

The Domain filter options should be fetched dynamically from the API endpoint:

*API Endpoint:*

 
{code:java}
GET https://${gateway-host-name}/pinxt-selfservice/v1/tags?categoryName=Domain{code}
h2. Detailed Requirements
h3. 1. Filter Chip Behavior (Mutually Exclusive)

*Rule:* Only ONE of the three filters can be active at any given time.
 * follow the selected/un-selected black/gray styling from existing implementation 

h3. 2. Domain Filter Chip Display States

*State 1: No Selection (Default)*
{code:java}
Display: "Domain"
Style: Refer to mock
Behavior: Click to open dropdown {code}
{*}State 2: Single Domain Selected{*}{*}{{*}}
{code:java}
Display: "Domain: Ordering"
Format: [Label] : [Value]
Style: Refer to mock
Elements: Dropdown arrow (▼) + Close button (×)
Behavior: 
  - Click chip body → Open dropdown to edit
  - Click × → Clear filter, return to View All
  - Hover → No tooltip needed {code}
*State 3: Multiple Domains Selected*
{code:java}
Display: "Domain: 3 selected"
Format: [Label] : [Count] selected
Style: Refer to Mock
Elements: Dropdown arrow (▼) + Close button (×)
Behavior:
  - Click chip body → Open dropdown to edit
  - Click × → Clear filter, return to View All
  - Hover → Show tooltip with all selected domain names (comma-separated) {code}
h3. 3. Domain Dropdown Behavior

*Opening the Dropdown:*
 * Click on Domain chip/button
 * Dropdown appears below the chip
 * Shows all 16 domain options with checkboxes
 * Previously selected domains are pre-checked

*Selecting Domains:*
 * Users can check/uncheck multiple domains
 * No limit on number of selections
 * Checkboxes remain interactive while dropdown is open

*Closing the Dropdown:*

*Option A: Click "Apply" Button*
 * Applies the current checkbox selections
 * Closes the dropdown
 * Updates the Domain chip display
 * Sets Domain as the active filter (black chip)

*Option B: Click Outside Dropdown*
 * Auto-applies the current checkbox selections
 * Closes the dropdown
 * Updates the Domain chip display
 * Sets Domain as the active filter (black chip)

*Option C: Click "Clear" Button*
 * Unchecks all checkboxes in the dropdown
 * Does NOT close the dropdown
 * Allows user to start fresh selection

*Option D: Click × on Domain Chip*
 * Clears all domain selections
 * Closes dropdown if open
 * Returns to View All as active filter

h3. 5. Tooltip Behavior (Multi-Select Only)

*When to Show:*
 * Only when 2+ domains are selected
 * On hover over the Domain chip

*Content:*
 * Comma-separated list of all selected domain names
 * Example: "Ordering, Identity & Shared Services, Wireless"

h3. 6. Filter Reset Logic

*Critical Behavior:* When switching between filters, domain selections must be cleared and mutually exclusive logic needs to be applied to unselected filters.
h2. Acceptance Criteria
h3. AC1: Filter Chip Mutual Exclusivity
 * [ ] Only one filter (View All, Favorites, or Domain) can be active/black at a time
 * [ ] Active filter / Inactive filters styling matches with existing implementation.
 * [ ] Clicking View All deactivates Favorites and clears Domain selections
 * [ ] Clicking Favorites deactivates View All and clears Domain selections
 * [ ] Selecting Domain(s) deactivates View All and Favorites

h3. AC2: Domain Filter - No Selection State
 * [ ] Domain chip displays text "Domain"
 * [ ] Domain chip has gray background and dark text
 * [ ] Domain chip has dropdown arrow (▼)
 * [ ] No close button (×) is visible
 * [ ] Clicking chip opens dropdown with all 16 domain options
 * [ ] All checkboxes are unchecked

h3. AC3: Domain Filter - Single Selection State
 * [ ] Domain chip displays "Domain: [DomainName]" format
 * [ ] Domain chip has black background and white text
 * [ ] Domain chip shows dropdown arrow (▼) and close button (×)
 * [ ] Clicking chip body opens dropdown with selected domain pre-checked
 * [ ] Clicking × clears selection and returns to View All
 * [ ] No tooltip appears on hover

h3. AC4: Domain Filter - Multiple Selection State
 * [ ] Domain chip displays "Domain: X selected" where X is the count
 * [ ] Domain chip has black background and white text
 * [ ] Domain chip shows dropdown arrow (▼) and close button (×)
 * [ ] Clicking chip body opens dropdown with all selected domains pre-checked
 * [ ] Clicking × clears all selections and returns to View All
 * [ ] Hovering over chip shows tooltip with comma-separated list of all selected domains
 * [ ] Tooltip appears above the chip with dark background

h3. AC5: Domain Dropdown - Opening and Display
 * [ ] Dropdown appears below the Domain chip when clicked
 * [ ] Dropdown shows header "Select Domains"
 * [ ] All 16 domain options are displayed with checkboxes
 * [ ] Previously selected domains are pre-checked when dropdown opens
 * [ ] Dropdown has white background with shadow
 * [ ] Dropdown min-width is 320px

h3. AC6: Domain Dropdown - Selection Interaction
 * [ ] Users can check multiple domains (no limit)
 * [ ] Users can uncheck domains
 * [ ] Checkbox state changes immediately on click
 * [ ] Hover over domain option shows light gray background
 * [ ] Clicking checkbox or label toggles selection
 * [ ] If many domains, dropdown is scrollable (max-height: 350px)

h3. AC7: Domain Options - Dynamic Loading
 * [ ] Domain options are fetched from API on page load
 * [ ] API endpoint: {{GET [https://${gateway-host-name}/pinxt-selfservice/v1/tags?categoryName=Domain|https://apis-internal-corp.shared.dev-spectrum.net/pinxt-selfservice/v1/tags?categoryName=Domain]}}
 * [ ] While loading, dropdown shows "Loading domains..." message
 * [ ] If API fails, dropdown shows error message
 * [ ] Domain options are rendered dynamically from API response
 * [ ] Domain list is sorted alphabetically 
 * [ ] If API returns empty list, show appropriate message

h3. AC8: Domain Dropdown - Apply Button
 * [ ] Apply button has black background and white text
 * [ ] Apply button text is "Apply"
 * [ ] Clicking Apply applies current checkbox selections
 * [ ] Clicking Apply closes the dropdown
 * [ ] Clicking Apply updates Domain chip display
 * [ ] Clicking Apply sets Domain as active filter (black chip)

h3. AC8: Domain Dropdown - Clear Button
 * [ ] Clear button has white background with black border
 * [ ] Clear button text is "Clear"
 * [ ] Clicking Clear unchecks all checkboxes
 * [ ] Clicking Clear does NOT close the dropdown
 * [ ] User can continue selecting after clicking Clear

h3. AC9: Domain Dropdown - Auto-Apply on Click Outside
 * [ ] Clicking outside dropdown applies current selections
 * [ ] Clicking outside dropdown closes the dropdown
 * [ ] Clicking outside updates Domain chip display
 * [ ] Clicking outside sets Domain as active filter if selections exist
 * [ ] Clicking on View All or Favorites while dropdown is open closes dropdown and clears selections

h3. AC10: Domain Dropdown - Close Button (×) on Chip
 * [ ] Close button only appears when Domain has selections
 * [ ] Clicking × clears all domain selections
 * [ ] Clicking × closes dropdown if open
 * [ ] Clicking × resets Domain chip to default gray state
 * [ ] Clicking × sets View All as active filter
 * [ ] Clicking × does not trigger dropdown open

h3. AC11: Filter Reset When Switching
 * [ ] Selecting View All clears any Domain selections
 * [ ] Selecting Favorites clears any Domain selections
 * [ ] Domain checkboxes are unchecked when View All is selected
 * [ ] Domain checkboxes are unchecked when Favorites is selected
 * [ ] Domain chip returns to default "Domain" text when cleared

h3. AC12: Tooltip Behavior
 * [ ] Tooltip only appears when 2+ domains are selected
 * [ ] Tooltip shows on hover over Domain chip
 * [ ] Tooltip displays comma-separated list of all selected domains
 * [ ] Tooltip text styling is consistent with other areas of app.
 * [ ] Tooltip appears above the chip
 * [ ] Tooltip has arrow pointing to chip
 * [ ] Tooltip disappears when mouse leaves chip

h3. AC13: Visual Styling Consistency
 * [ ] All filter chips have consistent
 * [ ] Dropdown buttons match reference styling
 * [ ] Hover states are implemented for all interactive elements

h3. AC14: Responsive Behavior
 * [ ] Dropdown positioning adjusts if near viewport edge
 * [ ] Tooltip doesn't overflow viewport
 * [ ] Filter chips wrap to new line if needed on smaller screens
 * [ ] Dropdown is scrollable if content exceeds max-height

